{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T18:59:10.397441+00:00", "event": "tool_response", "tool": "get_node_definition_detail", "response": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"id\":\"server\",\"boot\":{\"timeout\":20,\"completed\":[\"###### BOOT CONFIG DONE ######\"]},\"sim\":{\"linux_native\":{\"libvirt_domain_driver\":\"kvm\",\"driver\":\"server\",\"disk_driver\":\"virtio\",\"ram\":128,\"cpus\":1,\"cpu_limit\":100,\"nic_driver\":\"virtio\",\"boot_disk_size\":16,\"video\":{\"memory\":16}}},\"general\":{\"nature\":\"server\",\"description\":\"Tiny Core Linux\",\"read_only\":true},\"configuration\":{\"generator\":{\"driver\":\"server\"},\"provisioning\":{\"files\":[{\"editable\":true,\"name\":\"iosxe_config.txt\",\"content\":\"# this is a shell script which will be sourced at boot\\nhostname inserthostname-here\\n# configurable user account\\nUSERNAME=cisco\\nPASSWORD=cisco\\n# no password for tc user by default\\nTC_PASSWORD=\\n\"}],\"media_type\":\"iso\",\"volume_name\":\"cfg\"}},\"device\":{\"interfaces\":{\"serial_ports\":1,\"physical\":[\"eth0\",\"eth1\",\"eth2\",\"eth3\",\"eth4\",\"eth5\",\"eth6\",\"eth7\",\"eth8\",\"eth9\"],\"has_loopback_zero\":false,\"default_count\":1}},\"ui\":{\"label_prefix\":\"server-\",\"icon\":\"server\",\"label\":\"Server\",\"visible\":true,\"group\":\"Others\",\"description\":\"Tiny Core Linux\\n\\n128 MB DRAM, 1 vCPU\\n\\n##### Configuration\\nShell commands in the configuration field of the\\nnode are just sourced as user `root` when the node\\nstarts up. Tiny Core Linux is pretty much a RAM disk\\nbased distribution; unless a backup is initiated using\\nthe `backup` command, there's nothing saved when\\nrestarting / reloading a node. The default username\\nis `tc` without a password. There is also a user\\n`cisco` with password `cisco`. Additional packages\\ncan be installed using the interactive `tce` command.\\nThis, of course, requires external connectivity to\\nreach the repo servers. For further information click\\n[here](http://www.tinycorelinux.net/concepts.html).\\n\\n##### Example\\n```shell\\nhostname server-0\\nifconfig eth1 10.0.0.1 netmask 255.255.255.0 up\\nroute add -net 10.0.0.0/8 dev eth1\\n```\"},\"inherited\":{\"image\":{\"ram\":true,\"cpus\":true,\"data_volume\":true,\"boot_disk_size\":true,\"cpu_limit\":true},\"node\":{\"ram\":true,\"cpus\":true,\"data_volume\":true,\"boot_disk_size\":true,\"cpu_limit\":true}},\"pyats\":{\"os\":\"linux\"},\"schema_version\":\"0.0.1\"}", "annotations": null, "meta": null}], "structured_content": {"id": "server", "boot": {"timeout": 20, "completed": ["###### BOOT CONFIG DONE ######"]}, "sim": {"linux_native": {"libvirt_domain_driver": "kvm", "driver": "server", "disk_driver": "virtio", "ram": 128, "cpus": 1, "cpu_limit": 100, "nic_driver": "virtio", "boot_disk_size": 16, "video": {"memory": 16}}}, "general": {"nature": "server", "description": "Tiny Core Linux", "read_only": true}, "configuration": {"generator": {"driver": "server"}, "provisioning": {"files": [{"editable": true, "name": "iosxe_config.txt", "content": "# this is a shell script which will be sourced at boot\nhostname inserthostname-here\n# configurable user account\nUSERNAME=cisco\nPASSWORD=cisco\n# no password for tc user by default\nTC_PASSWORD=\n"}], "media_type": "iso", "volume_name": "cfg"}}, "device": {"interfaces": {"serial_ports": 1, "physical": ["eth0", "eth1", "eth2", "eth3", "eth4", "eth5", "eth6", "eth7", "eth8", "eth9"], "has_loopback_zero": false, "default_count": 1}}, "ui": {"label_prefix": "server-", "icon": "server", "label": "Server", "visible": true, "group": "Others", "description": "Tiny Core Linux\n\n128 MB DRAM, 1 vCPU\n\n##### Configuration\nShell commands in the configuration field of the\nnode are just sourced as user `root` when the node\nstarts up. Tiny Core Linux is pretty much a RAM disk\nbased distribution; unless a backup is initiated using\nthe `backup` command, there's nothing saved when\nrestarting / reloading a node. The default username\nis `tc` without a password. There is also a user\n`cisco` with password `cisco`. Additional packages\ncan be installed using the interactive `tce` command.\nThis, of course, requires external connectivity to\nreach the repo servers. For further information click\n[here](http://www.tinycorelinux.net/concepts.html).\n\n##### Example\n```shell\nhostname server-0\nifconfig eth1 10.0.0.1 netmask 255.255.255.0 up\nroute add -net 10.0.0.0/8 dev eth1\n```"}, "inherited": {"image": {"ram": true, "cpus": true, "data_volume": true, "boot_disk_size": true, "cpu_limit": true}, "node": {"ram": true, "cpus": true, "data_volume": true, "boot_disk_size": true, "cpu_limit": true}}, "pyats": {"os": "linux"}, "schema_version": "0.0.1"}, "meta": null}}
